<mxCell id="q2c35" value="from collections import deque&lt;br&gt;queue = deque([start])&lt;br&gt;node = queue.popleft()   # the one-line fix" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=11;fillColor=#272822;fontColor=#f8f8f2;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="334" width="520" height="64" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="q2c36" value="&lt;b&gt;Answer:&lt;/b&gt; each pop(0) is O(N), so BFS can degrade to O(V²). Use collections.deque with popleft(): O(1), restoring O(V + E)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=13;align=left;spacingLeft=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="414" width="820" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
