<mxCell id="q9c17" value="Keep indices with increasing heights. At i = 4 (height 2), pop 6: left boundary 2, width 4 − 2 − 1 = 1 → area 6. Pop 5: left boundary 1, width 4 − 1 − 1 = 2 → &lt;b&gt;area 10&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A sentinel height 0 at the end pops everything that remains." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="500" y="130" width="360" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="q9c18" value="&lt;b&gt;Answer:&lt;/b&gt; area 10 (height 5, width 2). Each popped bar&#x27;s rectangle spans from the new stack top to the current index. O(N): each bar pushed and popped once." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=13;align=left;spacingLeft=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="360" width="820" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
